      "created_at": "2026-10-18T17:18:51Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-18T17:18:51Z",
      "body": "Thanks for checking this so carefully — you're right. With OkHttp 5.5.0 and no `connectionSpecs` override, `MODERN_TLS` already limits every socket to TLS 1.2/1.3 before the handshake, so the wrapper only repeats what OkHttp does. RVSec's rule only looks at the literal passed to `SSLContext.getInstance` and can't see OkHttp's per-socket filtering, so this is a false positive for the OkHttp path. I'll close the PR — sorry for the noise, and thanks for the clear explanation.",
